{{!
    @template theme_baz/sidebar-support

    Support contact at the foot of the sidebar.

    The email and phone used to live only inside the floating "Need help?"
    panel, which ships hidden behind a button and is rendered by the student
    shells alone. Staff therefore had no route to support anywhere in the UI,
    and students had to know to open the panel. Here it is simply present, on
    every page, for every audience, with no interaction required.

    The markup comes from theme_baz_support_contact() via the shared template
    context, so the panel and the sidebar cannot disagree about the contact
    details. Renders nothing when a site has published neither.

    Context variables required for this template:
    * hassidebarsupport - whether the site published an email or phone
    * sidebarsupport - the contact markup

    Example context (json):
    {
        "hassidebarsupport": true,
        "sidebarsupport": "<div class=\"sw-help-contact\">…</div>"
    }
}}
{{#hassidebarsupport}}
<div class="sd-sidesupport">{{{ sidebarsupport }}}</div>
{{/hassidebarsupport}}
